from pathlib import Path
import json,html,sys
r=Path(sys.argv[1]);tele=json.loads((r/'telemetry.json').read_text());rows=''
for t in tele:
 u=t['usage'] or {};rows+=f"<tr><td>{t['arm'].title()}</td><td>{t['phase']}</td>"+''.join(f"<td>{u.get(k,0):,}</td>" for k in ['input_tokens','cached_input_tokens','uncached_input_tokens','output_tokens'])+f"<td>{t['seconds']/60:.1f}</td></tr>"
links='';gallery=''
for a in ['baseline','upgraded']:
 links+=f'<article><h3>{a.title()}</h3><p>{"Original skills, direct APIs and ordinary files" if a=="baseline" else "Same skills plus controller, MCP and memory"}</p><a class="button" href="{a}/report.html">Initial report →</a> <a class="button" href="{a}/followup.html">Fresh-session follow-up →</a></article>'
 figs=[p for p in (r/a).rglob('*.png') if 'preview' not in p.name]
 gallery+=f'<section><h2>{a.title()} · figure gallery</h2><div class="gallery">'
 for f in figs:
  rel=f.relative_to(r);label=f.stem.replace('_',' ').replace('-',' ')
  gallery+=f'<figure><a href="{rel}"><img src="{rel}" alt="{html.escape(label)}"></a><figcaption>{html.escape(label)} · open for full size and consult report captions</figcaption></figure>'
 gallery+='</div></section>'
summary=(r/'headline.txt').read_text() if (r/'headline.txt').exists() else 'Results and independent assessment are recorded below.'
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Kidney cancer · Two workflows, one dataset</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f2f5f8;color:#182f40;font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:40px 30px}header{padding:36px;border-radius:24px;background:linear-gradient(115deg,#142c46,#005965);color:white}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,54px);line-height:1.12;max-width:1000px}header p{max-width:950px}.eyebrow{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#9cddd1;font-weight:700}section{padding:28px;margin:25px 0;background:white;border:1px solid #dae4ed;border-radius:18px}.cards,.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px}article{padding:24px;border:1px solid #dce3ea;border-radius:14px}.button{display:inline-block;background:#006a75;color:white;padding:9px 14px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;margin:8px 6px 0 0}a{color:#006674}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{text-align:right;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce3ea}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}.scroll{overflow:auto}figure{margin:0}img{width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #e3e8ed}figcaption{font-size:14px;color:#566d7c;margin:8px 0}.note{border-left:4px solid #b66b2c;padding-left:18px}@media(max-width:800px){.cards,.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding:18px}header,section{padding:22px}}
</style><main><header><div class="eyebrow">CPTAC KIDNEY CANCER · PROTEOGENOMICS · MATCHED PILOT</div><h1>Two workflows.<br>One molecular dataset.</h1><p>From 110 downloaded tumors to 72 eligible patients with paired tumor/normal RNA and protein measurements. Two fresh agents, the same source access, and a fresh-session sensitivity analysis in 37 early-stage cases.</p><p>Original skills versus controller + MCP + memory. Jev excluded. Exploratory research; no treatment-efficacy or causal claims.</p></header><section><h2>What we learned</h2><p>'''+html.escape(summary)+'''</p><p class="note">One pair of runs cannot establish a general efficiency advantage. Data processing, evidence interpretation and visual quality are evaluated separately from runtime compliance.</p><a href="README.md">Full interpretation and limitations</a> · <a href="independent_review.md">Independent scientific review</a></section><section><h2>How MCP supports the analysis</h2><a href="mcp_analysis_diagram.svg"><img src="mcp_analysis_diagram.svg" alt="MCP connects a molecular shortlist to protein annotations, target evidence, literature and trial records; source snapshots support traceable interpretation, while local statistics and independent review remain separate."></a><p>MCP standardized retrieval and provenance in this study. Direct APIs can access the same evidence. Better interpretation depends on the analysis and review; this pilot did not demonstrate superior results or token savings.</p></section><section><h2>Explore the reports</h2><p class="note">The report and figure include the reviewed VEGFA count correction (1 all-stage / 0 early-stage). Original measured artifacts remain in the audit archive; token totals and review scores are unchanged.</p><div class="cards">'''+links+'''</div></section><section><h2>Actual model usage</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>Phase</th><th>Input</th><th>Cached input</th><th>Uncached input</th><th>Output</th><th>Minutes</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table></div><p>Cached input is a subset of total input; uncached = total − cached. These are accumulated model-call tokens, not the context-window size or billed dollars. Setup, reviewer and parent-orchestration usage are excluded. Both arms could reuse ordinary saved files and source snapshots.</p><a href="telemetry.json">Telemetry</a> · <a href="mcp_calls.json">Actual MCP calls</a> · <a href="initial_preservation.json">Initial-artifact preservation</a></section>'''+gallery+'''<section><h2>Evidence, with limits</h2><p>Processed matrices came from LinkedOmics; published CPTAC clinical annotations supplied histology and specimen exclusions. UniProt provides mappings and Reactome annotations; Open Targets supplies tractability and drug/candidate records across indications. Literature and trial records require independent interpretation. Pathway annotation is not enrichment, and a drug-target link is not kidney-cancer efficacy.</p><a href="source_guide.md">Shared source guide</a> · <a href="review_protocol.md">Frozen evaluation rubric</a> · <a href="protocol.json">Experiment protocol</a></section></main></html>'''
(r/'index.html').write_text(page)
